            <ArticleTitle>Postural headache and cerebrospinal fluid leak: believing is seeing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>681; discussion 681</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 33-year-old woman developed persistent postural headache following epidural anesthesia (L2-L3 level). Iohexol myelography (L5-S1 puncture) demonstrated no epidural extravasation of contrast material (Figure A), but subsequent computed tomography (CT) axial images (B, C) revealed leakage of dye through the needle track of the L5-S1 puncture (arrows). No leakage of contrast medium was found at the site of the L2-L3 epidural puncture.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
